IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Credit Contracts and Consumer Finance Act 2003 (New Zealand) — THE NOUNS.
--
-- Every fact the rule modules read, and nothing else: no rules, no #EVAL.
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2003_52.txt (New Zealand
-- Legislation, version as at 1 July 2026, converted from the PCO XML).
-- Field names are unique across records.

§ `Credit Contracts and Consumer Finance Act 2003 — the nouns`

§§ `Cancellation (ss 27-29)`

DECLARE Cancellation HAS
    -- s 17 initial disclosure, if made.
    `initial disclosure made on`                        IS A MAYBE DATE
    `notice of cancellation given on`                   IS A DATE
    -- s 27(2): a credit sale of the kinds listed (goods possessed with the
    -- disclosure in Schedule 1(s), an auction, property or services the
    -- debtor wants to keep, services performed).
    `a credit sale of a kind in s 27(2)`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `cash price paid on`                                IS A MAYBE DATE
    `advance and property returned on`                  IS A MAYBE DATE
    -- s 29.
    `credit for less than 2 months, not refinancing the creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a layby sale agreement`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `cancellation Matariki days`                        IS A LIST OF DATE

§§ `Interest and high-cost credit (ss 39-45I)`

DECLARE `Default interest facts` HAS
    `amount in default that was due anyway`             IS A NUMBER
    `amount made payable early because of the default`  IS A NUMBER
    `amount over the credit limit`                      IS A NUMBER
    `an on demand facility`                             IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `High-cost facts` HAS
    -- s 45C, in percent a year.
    `annual interest rate, percent`                     IS A NUMBER
    `highest weighted average annual rate, percent`     IS A NUMBER
    `highest cumulative rate on default or over-limit, percent` IS A NUMBER
    `of a class declared by the FMA`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 45F: the debtor's balances with other creditors' high-cost contracts.
    `has an unpaid balance with another high-cost creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `last day of a balance with another high-cost creditor` IS A MAYBE DATE
    -- s 45G: the dates the debtor entered into high-cost contracts.
    `high-cost contracts entered on`                    IS A LIST OF DATE
    -- ss 45F(2), 45G(2): reasonable inquiries and reasonable grounds.
    `the creditor has the s 45F or 45G defence`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `provides for compound interest`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 45E.
    `first advance`                                     IS A NUMBER
    `costs of borrowing so far across related contracts` IS A NUMBER

§§ `Hardship (ss 55-57A)`

DECLARE `Hardship application` HAS
    `hardship application made on`                      IS A DATE
    `previous application made on`                      IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the creditor agrees to consider it`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasons materially different from before`          IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 57(1)(a).
    `days in default after a repossession warning notice` IS A NUMBER
    `consecutive periodic payments missed`              IS A NUMBER
    `in default since`                                  IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the default has been remedied`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 57(1)(b).
    `inability reasonably foreseeable when contracting` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Statutory damages (s 89)`

DECLARE `Kind of breach` IS ONE OF
    `s 9C(3)(a) no reasonable inquiries before the agreement`
    `s 9C(4)(a) no reasonable inquiries before a guarantee`
    `s 9C(5)(a) no reasonable inquiries before relevant insurance`
    `s 45F or 45G a prohibited high-cost contract`
    `s 18 continuing disclosure`
    `s 24 request disclosure`
    `s 25(1)(a) disclosure of a guarantee`
    `any other breach`

DECLARE `Kind of contract` IS ONE OF
    `a revolving credit contract`
    `a consumer lease`
    `another credit contract`
    `a buy-back transaction`

DECLARE Breach HAS
    `kind of breach`                                    IS A `Kind of breach`
    `kind of contract`                                  IS A `Kind of contract`
    -- the amount s 89 measures for this kind of breach: the interest charges
    -- and fees payable (for the period that applies), the amount paid, or —
    -- for s 25(1)(a) and other breaches — the base for the 5%.
    `amount measured`                                   IS A NUMBER
    -- s 89(1A): a revolving credit contract with no credit limit.
    `a revolving contract without a credit limit`       IS A BOOLEAN
